Z||000000||Sootah||10-15-2001||06:54 PM||||Thats pretty much all that I want to know. If I've got to do this (And, I do.) I may as well make it a 3.4 since I've heard that they are easy to do. This is the route I am going to go unless somebody in here wants to donate me a running engine; Not neccisarily a totally insane consept. There are members here that have recently done swaps. I'll pay shipping!<P>Anyway, since the plea for a free engine prolly won't pan out, how do I go about finding the block and all that? Keep in mind, I am poor.<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Sootah__Nuclear_Happy_Face_Sig.jpg">     <BR><sup><I>Never pull your pants down in Cosco, the dang monkeys will getcha</I></sup> <BR><sup><B>AIM</B>: KSSouter</sup>||||reg||5
Z||000001||88formula||10-15-2001||07:15 PM||||The 93-95 Camaro is the car with the 3.4 you want. The hardest part will be relocating the starter. <P>If cost is really a concern for you than I would just find a good used 2.8-liter motor and swap that back in. That would be the cheapest way. The 3.4 swap isn’t exactly all plug and play! <BR><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||dennis_6||10-15-2001||07:21 PM||||I would put either a 3.4 Fbody engine (camaro,firebird)or a 3.1L FWD block.  The 3.1 might be easier.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Cooter||10-15-2001||08:03 PM||||Would the mini van 3.1 be a good choice? It is an iron head engine so the Fiero goodies should fit easily?||||reg||1
